From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Istvan Zoltan Ballok <istvan.zoltan.ballok@sap.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jan 2025 16:28:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] Remove the string literal assertion from the unit test

It is probably too long and not worth to keep it in the source code.

The remaining assertions
  Expect(result.NumberOfPathsChecked).To(Equal(36))
  Expect(result.NumberOfPathsWithFailedAssertion).To(Equal(0))
are sufficient to check to catch regressions when a race condition
would be introduced in the future.

The output of PathsChecked is helpful when checking a race condition
though.
---
